### Why recursive chains cannot hang

The unwind loop keeps a `seen` set of `funcIndex:pc` keys and a hard `guard` counter. When a tail-call link points at a key already in `seen`, the loop stops, marks the last emitted frame `recursive: true`, and returns — the correct behavior for a legitimate tail-recursive function and the safe behavior for adversarial input.
